From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eriko Kurimoto <elkurin@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 21:00:44 -0700
Subject: [FSA] Block /run in sensitive path blocklist

Add /run with kBlockAllChildren to the sensitive-directory blocklist on
Linux, ChromeOS, and Android.

This prevents sites from obtaining read/write directory access to per-
session runtime directories (such as /run/user/<uid>/dbus-1/services).

Bug: 577376424
Change-Id: I06035274613fb65514af217c92071c66785e446f
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8650678
Reviewed-by: Mingyu Lei <leimy@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Eriko Kurimoto <elkurin@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1727713}

Electron adaptation notes (44-x-y):
Electron's refactor_expose_file_system_access_blocklist.patch relocates the kBlockPaths table into chrome_file_system_access_permission_context.h, so the /run rule is added there (same position, after /etc).

diff --git a/chrome/browser/file_system_access/chrome_file_system_access_permission_context.h b/chrome/browser/file_system_access/chrome_file_system_access_permission_context.h
index 696cf3bef0ec2797bb4acfdf1cb54e8d2d670bf7..fafd956302128d0590a09ab82bff3bc07cea322a 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/file_system_access/chrome_file_system_access_permission_context.h
+++ b/chrome/browser/file_system_access/chrome_file_system_access_permission_context.h
@@ -706,6 +706,11 @@ class ChromeFileSystemAccessPermissionContext
                                   BlockType::kBlockAllChildren),
         BlockPath::CreateAbsolute(FILE_PATH_LITERAL("/etc"),
                                   BlockType::kBlockAllChildren),
+        // And runtime data in /run, including per-session runtime directories
+        // (/run/user/<uid>, the default $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR), see
+        // crbug.com/577376424.
+        BlockPath::CreateAbsolute(FILE_PATH_LITERAL("/run"),
+                                  BlockType::kBlockAllChildren),
         // Block ~/.dbus as well, just in case, although there probably isn't much
         // a website can do with access to that directory and its contents.
         BlockPath::CreateRelative(base::DIR_HOME, FILE_PATH_LITERAL(".dbus"),
diff --git a/chrome/browser/file_system_access/chrome_file_system_access_permission_context_unittest.cc b/chrome/browser/file_system_access/chrome_file_system_access_permission_context_unittest.cc
index a111ad1d5d0455dd3451d865bbe19001280cb1d3..405f1510e9bfe315294019b153bfeafecf56d278 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/file_system_access/chrome_file_system_access_permission_context_unittest.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/file_system_access/chrome_file_system_access_permission_context_unittest.cc
@@ -896,6 +896,29 @@ TEST_F(ChromeFileSystemAccessPermissionContextTest,
                 permission_context(), PathInfo(FILE_PATH_LITERAL("/dev")),
                 HandleType::kDirectory, UserAction::kNone),
             SensitiveDirectoryResult::kAbort);
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX) || BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS) || BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID)
